    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`mock_openai()` works again and both digest tests pass (`pytest -q`: 2 passed). The only file changed is `tests/fakes.py`.\n\n**Cause:** openai 3.19.2 no longer sends requests through `httpx`. It uses a separate package, `httpx2` (with `httpcore2` underneath). respx 0.23.1 only patches `httpx`, so it never saw those requests, and since nothing was checking, they quietly went to the real network.\n\n**Fix:** Inside `mock_openai()`, a new helper `_route_httpx2_through(router)` replaces `httpx2.HTTPTransport.handle_request` for the length of the `with` block. It converts each request into an `httpx.Request`, sends it through the same respx router as before, and converts the reply back into an `httpx2.Response`. Because the patch is on the class rather than on one client, it catches:\n- clients created before the block, including app.digest's cached `get_client()`;\n- clients created inside the block;\n- clients given a plain `httpx.Client` as `http_client` (openai still accepts that), which respx itself still covers.\n\n`mock.patch.object` undoes the patch when the block exits. Unmatched requests still raise respx's `AllMockedAssertionError`, as they used to. The helper's interface and docstring are unchanged.\n\n**Checks:** I also ran a throwaway script that confirmed:\n- a client created before the block, one created inside it, and one using a plain `httpx.Client` each got their canned reply;\n- a fourth request got the 400 error;\n- all four request bodies were recorded.\n\nThe script ran outside pytest, where there is network access. After the block ended, the next request reached the real API and got a 401 for the dummy key, which shows nothing is intercepted afterwards.\n\nI didn't use `httpx2.alias_httpx()`. It changes the imports for the whole process, can't be undone, and fails anyway because `httpx` is already imported.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** deleting the scratch file `_scratch_check.py` in the project root needed your approval, so it's still there. Please delete it."
  },
